cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this exploratory research archive, cite this software and the
  relevant methods and dependencies listed in ATTRIBUTION.md. The archive
  does not establish an end-to-end latency or accuracy advantage.
type: software
title: "Learned BP for bivariate bicycle codes: exploratory research archive"
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Turan
    given-names: Berkay Barış
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducible experiments on learned min-sum belief propagation with BP-OSD
  fallback for bivariate bicycle codes. Includes saved configurations, seeds,
  model snapshots, paired outcomes, audits, negative results and a feasibility
  assessment. Development is paused. Modest first-stage gains were observed;
  preserved logical accuracy and an end-to-end latency advantage over strong
  controls were not established.
